<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Finalborgo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Finalborgo is a walled medieval town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liguria">Liguria</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, now part of the municipality of Finale Ligure. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/del-carretto">Del Carretto</a> marquises of Finale, whose castle of Gavone stands on the hill above it. Its walls, gates and the former convent of Santa Caterina survive well.</p></div>
